@startuml
title BO — appointment lifecycle (made / no-show / cancel / reschedule / nail art)

actor Staff
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js BO)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

' All endpoints below are gated by IsStaffMember (role staff/admin).

== Load the calendar (range query) ==
Staff -> FE : open calendar (FullCalendar)
FE -> NGINX : GET /bo/v1/appointments/?staff_id&start_at&end_at  (Cookie: sessionid)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  appointments.views.BoAppointmentListView (IsStaffMember)
  staff_id + start_at + end_at are all REQUIRED
  appointments.selectors.list_staff_appointments_in_range()
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT appointments (staff, range)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer[])

== Mark made ==
Staff -> FE : mark appointment made
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/made/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : appointments.services.mark_made()
note over BE : only a booked appointment can be marked made
BE -> DB : UPDATE appointment (status=made)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer)

== Mark no-show ==
Staff -> FE : mark no-show
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/no-show/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : appointments.services.mark_no_show()
note over BE
  only a booked appointment can be a no-show.
  No-shows are tracked for analytics/reporting only —
  no automatic penalty or block in v1 (business-rules.md).
end note
BE -> DB : UPDATE appointment (status=no_show)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer)

== Cancel (staff) ==
Staff -> FE : cancel appointment
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/cancel/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : appointments.services.cancel_appointment(reason=staff)
note over BE
  Business rules (see business-rules.md):
  - not already canceled / completed (made / no_show)
  - sets status=canceled, cancel_reason=staff
  - staff cancellations are NOT bound by the 24h self-service cutoff
  - frees the time -> waitlist alert (_alert_waitlist)
end note
BE -> DB : UPDATE appointment (status=canceled, cancel_reason=staff)
BE -> BE : notifications.notify_waitlist_for_freed_time()
BE -> DB : SELECT waitlist ; INSERT notifications_boalert (if anyone waiting)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer, status=canceled)

== Reschedule (staff) ==
Staff -> FE : drag/drop to a new time
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/reschedule/ { new_start_at }  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  appointments.serializers.RescheduleSerializer.is_valid()
end note
BE -> BE : appointments.services.reschedule_appointment(by_client=False)
note over BE
  Business rules:
  - only a booked appointment; status STAYS booked (NOT a cancellation,
    so never counted as canceled in reports — business-rules.md)
  - re-validates booking window + working schedule at the new time
  - locks the staff row (_lock_staff) and re-checks for overlap
  - frees the OLD start for the waitlist (alert at freed time)
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (staff row) ; UPDATE appointment (start_at/end_at)
BE -> DB : SELECT waitlist ; INSERT notifications_boalert (if anyone waiting)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer, status=booked)

== Edit Nail Art (staff-only) ==
Staff -> FE : switch Nail Art simple <-> complex
FE -> NGINX : PATCH /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/nail-art/ { nail_art_option }  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  appointments.serializers.NailArtEditSerializer.is_valid()
end note
BE -> BE : appointments.services.edit_nail_art()
note over BE
  Business rules (see business-rules.md):
  - STAFF can change Nail Art; clients cannot (client app shows a
    "talk to staff" modal — see edit-nail-art-blocked.puml)
  - service must support Nail Art; appointment must be booked
  - recomputes duration (+15 simple / +30 complex) and end_at
  - locks staff row + re-checks overlap for the new duration
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (staff row) ; UPDATE appointment (nail_art, end_at, duration snapshot)
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer)
FE --> Staff : calendar refreshed
@enduml
